  "interpretation": "Of 4 delay-blind contrasts, 3 yield non-zero implied slips (all positive, +0.087 to +0.095) and 1 is consistent with zero (bounding the slip to <~11% at 2-sigma for that geometry). The pooled delay-blind slip is 7.8 +/- 2.0% with chi2 = 2.06 on 3 dof (p = 0.56): the measured and bounding directions are mutually consistent with a common order-percent slip. The negative-direction census counts 12 per-model slips with negative sign out of 36 model contrasts, of which 5 exceed 1-sigma \u2014 dominated by the free-form WSLAP+ models over-predicting the Encore and H0pe delays and by the strictly-blind Jauzac15.1 variant; every ensemble-level weighted mean remains positive. Measured slips sit at the measured mundane floor (median kappa_ext half-width 3.0%, SDSS1206 family spread ~6%), commensurate with the systematic the mechanism predicts the slip to masquerade as."
}